# Pressable GitHub deployment rules (gitignore-like syntax).
#
# Pressable deploys with "Sync-As-Is": files on the server that are NOT in this
# repository are DELETED from the destination path. This file assumes the
# deployment is configured with BOTH "Repository Subdirectory" and
# "Destination Path" left blank (repository root = /htdocs).
#
# Matched paths are neither deployed nor deleted on the server, so the allowlist
# below limits the deployment to this repository's theme and plugin, and keeps
# everything else on the server (WooCommerce and other plugins, languages,
# mu-plugins, files placed via SFTP, etc.) untouched.
#
# When you commit another theme or plugin to this repository, add a "!" line for
# it in the matching block below, and open its runtime files in the same way as
# pressable-theme / pressable-plugin (see "Inside our theme and plugin").
#
# When you add a file or folder directly under the theme or the plugin, add a "!"
# line for it, or it is not deployed. CI checks this (bin/check-deployignore.sh).

# ---- Allowlist: deploy only our theme and plugin ----
# Everything directly under the site root except wp-content/.
/*
!wp-content/

# The wp-content/ lines follow the style of Pressable's documented examples
# (no leading slash; the slash in the middle anchors them to the root), so they
# keep protecting the server even if a leading "/" is not supported.
wp-content/*
!wp-content/themes/
!wp-content/plugins/

wp-content/themes/*
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/

wp-content/plugins/*
!wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/

# ---- Inside our theme and plugin: deploy only the runtime files ----
# Seen on 2026-10-27 on the production of a site made from this template:
# CLAUDE.md, src/ and package-lock.json in the theme and plugin were deployed
# although "Development files" below lists them. Inferred from that: Pressable
# does not apply such later lines inside a directory that a "!" line brought
# back.
#
# So each directory is closed again with "<dir>/*" right after "!<dir>/", and
# only its runtime files are reopened. This is the shape of the levels above
# ("wp-content/*" after "!wp-content/", which keeps WooCommerce on the server),
# one level deeper. Not verified on Pressable yet: this shape at this depth, and
# reopening a single file (style.css, functions.php, pressable-plugin.php, ...).
# Check both on a staging site before relying on them, and update this comment.
#
# Reopen only what is in the repository: a "!" line for a missing file would
# un-protect a file with that name on the server, and Sync-As-Is would delete it
# (bin/check-deployignore.sh checks this). When you add screenshot.png, add its
# line too.
wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/*
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/assets/
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/functions.php
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/parts/
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/patterns/
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/style.css
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/styles/
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/templates/
!wp-content/themes/pressable-theme/theme.json

wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/*
!wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/build/
!wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/includes/
!wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/pressable-plugin.php

# ---- Development files (never deployed) ----
# Repository root files are already covered by "/*"; they are listed again so
# they are not published even if "/*" is not supported. Inside the theme and
# the plugin, these lines did not keep CLAUDE.md, src/ or package-lock.json out
# (see above), so files there are kept out by not reopening them. .DS_Store and
# *.log never reach the repository (.gitignore), so they are not deployed.
.DS_Store
**/*.log
.claude/
.deployignore
.editorconfig
.github/
.gitignore
.phpcs.xml.dist
CLAUDE.md
README.md
bin/*
composer.json
composer.lock
docs/
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
.nvmrc
wp-content/plugins/pressable-plugin/src/
